      "writtenOn": "2017-12-13T23:41:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes this \"long BLAKE2b\" hash construction is in the spec.\nSee 3.2 Operation - Point: \"Variable-length hash function\".\n\n\u003eSay that len(out) \u003d\u003d 65. The loop above will run twice and write 64 bytes of hash. This expression will be 33 and, since b2.Sum will want to append 33 bytes to out[:0] on line 52, it might a) write elsewhere and return a new slice or b) write past |out|, surprising the caller.\n\nNo,it will write 32 bytes to out, not enter the loop (out \u003d out[32:]) and than compute the last block like this: hashsize \u003d 33 + ((65 + 31) % 32) \u003d 33. The result is a 65 byte hash.\nI agree that the computation looks a bit odd and I change it to a version which is closer to the spec.",
      "parentUuid": "812e4e90_14df352d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 39
      },
